quran[25]{c,v,t}:
  26,112,He said: ‘What knowledge do I have about what they used to do?
  26,113,Their account is only with my Lord if you could perceive (what is true honour)!
  26,114,And I am not going to drive the believers away.
  26,115,I am just a manifest warner.’
  26,116,"They said: ‘If you do not stop (your preaching), O Nuh (Noah), you shall indeed be stoned (to death).’"
  26,117,"He said: ‘My Lord! Indeed, my people have rejected me."
  26,118,"So judge between me and them, and deliver me and the believers who are with me!’"
  26,119,So We delivered him and those with him in the fully laden Ark.
  26,120,Then We drowned the rest afterwards.
  26,121,"There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them are not believers."
  26,122,"And indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,123,"(The people of) ‘Ad rejected the messengers,"
  26,124,when their (kinship) brother Hud said to them: ‘Will you not be God-conscious?
  26,125,"Indeed, I am a trustworthy messenger (sent) to you."
  26,126,So be God-conscious and obey me.
  26,127,And I do not ask you for any reward for this (message). My reward lies only with the Lord of all worlds.
  26,128,Do you frivolously build on every prominent place a monument?
  26,129,You construct castles as if you will live (in the world) forever.
  26,130,"And whenever you seize (someone for punishment), you seize like ruthless tyrants."
  26,131,So be God-conscious and obey me.
  26,132,"And be conscious of Him, Who has provided you with (all the good things) that you know."
  26,133,"He has aided you with (an abundance of) cattle and children,"
  26,134,and gardens and springs.
  26,135,"Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a grievous day.’"
  26,136,They said: ‘It is the same to us whether you warn us or be not among the warners.
